    {
      "id": "d2ssu8d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Gram Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "861rrjb",
      "content": "• Consists of all registered voters in the village."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "65oqb12",
      "content": "• Acts as the foundation of the Panchayati Raj system."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yvv8pxk",
      "content": "• Approves plans and budgets of the Gram Panchayat."
    },
    {
      "id": "3ht7uzv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Gram Panchayat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lf14xl2",
      "content": "• Executive body at village level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lbkst3h",
      "content": "• Members elected directly by villagers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "unkjoro",
      "content": "• The head is called Sarpanch or Pradhan."
    },
    {
      "id": "ei4rg4d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Panchayat Samiti"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Level",
        "Governance Body",
        "Jurisdiction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Village Level",
          "Gram Panchayat",
          "Single village or group of villages"
        ],
        [
          "Block Level",
          "Panchayat Samiti",
          "Intermediate block region"
        ],
        [
          "District Level",
          "Zila Parishad",
          "Entire rural district"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "yo6t3ja"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x05yn38",
      "content": "• Works at block level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "93hm9e0",
      "content": "• Coordinates activities of Gram Panchayats."
    },
    {
      "id": "8vbzp0d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Zila Parishad"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5l6xyhr",
      "content": "• Functions at district level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3q87ems",
      "content": "• Supervises Panchayat Samitis."
    },
    {
      "id": "llptjft",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Key Features of the System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ht3pilo",
      "content": "• Three-tier structure of governance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ice4e5p",
      "content": "• Regular elections every five years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fltdqiw",
      "content": "• Reservation for SC, ST and women."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5yryi0m",
      "content": "• State Election Commission for conducting elections."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Part IX deals with the Panchayati Raj System in the Indian Constitution.",
        "The three tiers of governance are Gram Panchayat (Village level), Panchayat Samiti (Block level), and Zila Parishad (District level).",
        "Gram Sabha forms the foundational direct-democracy body of the Panchayati Raj framework."
      ],
      "id": "fm8qa1s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x2zv90p",
      "content": "• State Finance Commission for financial review."
    },
    {
      "id": "6ucoosw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "me1lveb",
      "content": "• 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act (1992) introduced Panchayati Raj."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ix5ubc",
      "content": "• Gram Sabha is the basic unit of rural democracy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dfqr04b",
      "content": "• At least one-third seats reserved for women."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1psic2u",
      "content": "• Panchayat elections are held every 5 years."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}